WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.228
Dr Hale has a new patient, Isla Penrose.

00:00:02.228 --> 00:00:08.800
She is fictional, and so are her three notes: an assessment written up in Word, a session follow-up, and a phone call.

00:00:09.404 --> 00:00:13.244
She gets a record on this Mac, which keeps her notes, documents and redactions together.

00:00:17.278 --> 00:00:19.313
The first note is a Word document.

00:00:19.313 --> 00:00:24.998
It is imported as text for me to check, and the original file is kept in the encrypted library.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:31.607
Finding identifiers takes well under a second, all on this Mac.

00:00:32.211 --> 00:00:33.923
Every proposal is my decision.

00:00:33.923 --> 00:00:37.517
I keep words that identify nobody, like the test banner and GP.

00:00:37.517 --> 00:00:42.196
Her first name turned up on its own, so I give it the same label as her full name.

00:00:42.196 --> 00:00:43.851
The rest become placeholders.

00:01:06.597 --> 00:01:10.877
Her reference number slipped through, so I select it and add it by hand.

00:01:11.665 --> 00:01:16.705
Saving the note also saves each decision as a redaction for Isla, ready for her next note.

00:01:22.007 --> 00:01:24.847
Two weeks later, the follow-up is pasted straight in.

00:01:27.107 --> 00:01:30.704
Her name is already replaced, from her saved redactions.

00:01:30.704 --> 00:01:35.907
Only what is new needs a decision: her partner, Tom, her employer, and the dates.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.190
A few decisions, and the second note is saved.

00:01:50.631 --> 00:01:53.511
The third note is a phone call, so I dictate it.

00:02:00.026 --> 00:02:02.383
Phone call with Isla Penrose this afternoon.

00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:05.490
She's sleeping through most nights now, and the three a.m.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.882
waking has nearly stopped.

00:02:06.882 --> 00:02:09.400
Tom has been a big help with the evening walks.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.346
She'd like to keep her session on the sixth of October.

00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:19.433
Whisper transcribed that here, and the audio was never saved.

00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:22.074
It goes through the same review as everything else.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:31.273
Three notes, captured three ways, with every saved redaction listed and editable.

00:02:31.273 --> 00:02:33.800
And her notes are searchable, right here.

00:02:36.094 --> 00:02:42.276
That was a patient's notes in Clinician's Veil: imported, pasted and dictated, every one de-identified on the Mac.

00:02:42.276 --> 00:02:47.374
Each note teaches it a little more about whom to hide, and the clinician decides every change.
